# =============================================================================
# OrCaNN .gitignore
#
# Design note: the data/, models/ and results/ trees are kept in git through
# small `*_<ext>.txt` placeholder files that document what belongs in each
# location. The heavy artefacts themselves (raw recordings, masks, trained
# weights, output arrays) live on the cluster / external storage and are NOT
# committed, so their binary extensions are ignored below. The placeholders are
# plain .txt and stay tracked, preserving the directory layout.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env

# --- Heavy data / model / output artefacts (kept off git; see .txt placeholders) ---
*.nd2
*.tif
*.tiff
*.npy
*.npz
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.zip
*.avi

# --- SGE / Grid Engine job logs (real cluster run output) ---
*.o[0-9]*
*.e[0-9]*
*.po[0-9]*
*.pe[0-9]*

# --- Local working notes and unverified code (not shared) ---
# dev/ holds design notes and scratch investigations that belong to whoever is
# working on the machine, not to the project: half-finished port plans, salvaged
# code paths, notes that point at files outside the repo. Keeping it ignored
# means it never has to be tidied before a commit. Anything in here that becomes
# a real design document should move into docs/ and be committed there.
/dev/

# src/orcann/dev/ is the code counterpart: analyses gated behind `analysis.dev`
# whose method is still being decided, held back until they have been checked
# against real recordings. The flag defaults to false and the call site is
# wrapped, so a checkout without this package behaves exactly as if the flag did
# not exist. An analysis graduates by being named below once it has been checked
# against real recordings — or better, by moving into orcann.analysis /
# orcann.figures and losing the flag with it.
src/orcann/dev/*
!src/orcann/dev/__init__.py
!src/orcann/dev/transient_decay.py

# Tool caches that land in the repo root (matplotlib font cache, etc.)
.cache/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Agent instructions and configuration (local, not part of the project) ---
# CLAUDE.md tells a coding agent how to work in this checkout: conventions,
# which conda env imports what, how reviews are run. .claude/ is the rest of the
# same thing -- agents, skills, settings and permissions for whoever is running
# one. Both describe a way of working rather than the pipeline itself, so they
# stay on the machine of whoever uses an agent and out of the shared history.
CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
.claude.json

# Manim render output and its scratch frames. The scenes in docs/anim/ are
# source; the mp4s they produce are not committed.
/videos/
docs/anim/_frames/
